cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  To cite the Awesome REA collection itself, use this metadata. It does not
  cite the papers, tools or other works listed in the collection: cite those
  from their own primary sources. When citing scan-derived counts, give the
  commit or snapshot date they come from.
title: Awesome Reverse Engineering Anything
type: dataset
version: 0.12.0
date-released: 2026-10-17
authors:
  - given-names: Yuxuan
    family-names: Zhang
    website: https://yuxuan.world/
  - given-names: Haozhe
    family-names: Wang
    website: https://haozheh3.github.io/
  - name: Awesome REA contributors
abstract: >-
  An independent, bilingual (English and Simplified Chinese) collection of
  source-reviewed tools, reconstruction cases and research papers for
  reverse engineering websites, games, apps, native binaries, firmware and
  communication protocols, with a separate automated index of scanned
  repository READMEs. Source review does not imply runtime verification.
url: https://awesomerea.org/
repository-code: https://github.com/reacher-z/Awesome-REA
license: MIT
keywords:
  - reverse engineering
  - decompilation
  - binary analysis
  - firmware analysis
  - protocol analysis
  - awesome list
